& [AuthorityInput] is sufficient for correction-candidate formation only
  + source identity is measured before SJS
  + I03D formation supplies the later library-source observation that requires correction
  + the original I03A package remains historical and inactive

& [Finding1] corrects interface absence
  + jsonschema 0.49.2 ValidationOptions owns a retriever even when default features are disabled
  + no-resolution must mean zero admitted retrieval capability and deterministic refusal rather than erased interface

& [Finding2] separates primary and sentinel controls
  + structural fragment-only preflight decides admissibility before library construction
  + a test-local zero-capability ProbeDenyRetriever guards the unavoidable library seam
  + retriever invocation is an internal fault rather than an ordinary rejection path

& [Finding3] keeps production ownership outside I03A
  + ProbeDenyRetriever exists only in the proposed focused integration test
  + production CantorDenyRetriever remains an I03D source obligation
  + I03A source-touch remains exactly the two Cargo manifests lock and one test

& [Finding4] makes construction semantics reproducible
  + Draft 2020-12 validate-formats false ignore-unknown-formats true zero custom formats and deny retriever are explicit
  + implicit library defaults are not authority

& [Finding5] corrects meta independence
  + meta result and instance result remain separate report identities
  + the supported public builder repeats schema validation
  + crate-private without_schema_validation cannot be part of the candidate

& [Finding6] preserves activation refusal
  + current Cargo.lock contains no jsonschema
  + no dependency source checksum feature build or host gate has been accepted
  + no satisfaction signature exists

& [AuditDisposition] is source_valid_after_refinement_revision_candidate_formation_allowed_activation_forbidden
